] [17592186437085 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186437073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437085 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "61f81261-3e5b-587f-b2ff-a3f22db029b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437086 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437086 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437086 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437086 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437086 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437086 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437086 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437086 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186437075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437086 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6a912a37-363a-53e6-bf86-dbe48185fc08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437087 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437087 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437087 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437087 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437087 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186437081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437087 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437087 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437087 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186437071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437087 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "843bf297-f481-59fb-a7e7-1153b03b247c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437088 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186437085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437088 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133394" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437088 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437088 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate ${f}_{xyz}(4,1,7)$ given that a function $f(x,y,z)$ and all of its higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ and that\n\n$$\n{f}_{xz}(x,y,z)=2x\\sqrt{z-3y}+z{e}^{x-4y}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437088 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "17f2fd35-823f-52a1-8bc6-17fa0dd0fd8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437088 #edb/ref 1074 "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(x,y,z) & ={f}_{xzy}(x,y,z) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{xz}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\sqrt{z-3y}+z{e}^{x-4y}) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{z-3y}})-4z{e}^{x-4y} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{z-3y}}-4z{e}^{x-4y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point  $(4,1,7):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(4,1,7) & =-\\frac{3\\cdot 4}{\\sqrt{7-3\\cdot 1}}-4\\cdot 7\\cdot {e}^{4-4\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{7-3}}-28{e}^{4-4} \\\\  & =-6-28 \\\\  & =-34\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437089 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186437086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437089 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133235" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437089 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437089 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(x,y)=2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+a{y}^{2},\\,{f}_{y}(x,y)=bx\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+6xy.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437089 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2a9101c-1b4a-5430-a447-8fae79ba4cdb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437089 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+a{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-2yx\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+2ay \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(bx\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+6xy) \\\\  & =b\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-bxy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+6y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-2yx\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+2ay & =b\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-bxy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+6y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $y$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),$ respectively, we see that $a=3$ and $b=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437090 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186437087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437090 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133224" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437090 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437090 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =a{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+5{y}^{2}-3, \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =b{x}^{3}y+10xy, \\\\ {f}_{x}(2,1) & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437090 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e1ce51ab-65e5-5a2f-a7f1-d19c74e60108" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186437090 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(a{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+5{y}^{2}-3) \\\\  & =2a{x}^{2}y+10y-0 \\\\  & =2a{x}^{2}y+10y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(b{x}^{3}y+10xy) \\\\  & =3b{x}^{2}y+10y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a{x}^{2}y+10y & =3b{x}^{2}y+10y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of ${x}^{2}y,$ we get $b=\\frac{2}{3}a.$ \n\nNow, since ${f}_{x}(2,1)=14$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(2,1) & =14 \\\\ a(2)^{2}(1)^{2}+5(1)^{2}-3 & =14 \\\\ 4a+2 & =14 \\\\ a & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $b=\\frac{2}{3}a=\\frac{2}{3}(3)=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
